  "domain": "spatial-computing",
  "definition": "Embodied AI Simulation is the practice of training, evaluating, and validating autonomous agents and robotic systems within physically accurate, interactive virtual environments before deployment on real hardware. These simulation platforms render high-fidelity physics (rigid and soft-body dynamics, fluid simulation, contact forces), sensor models (cameras, LiDAR, IMU, depth sensors), and procedurally generated scenes to expose agents to diverse scenarios at scale. Sim-to-real transfer methods \u2014 including domain randomisation, domain adaptation, and curriculum learning \u2014 are applied to close the fidelity gap between simulated and real-world conditions. The discipline spans household robot manipulation tasks, autonomous vehicle testing, humanoid locomotion, and multi-agent coordination, bridging artificial intelligence research with physical robotic deployment.",
